# Troubleshooting

Problems that came up during the workshop.

## A tool fails with a datatype error

The instructor estimated that most Galaxy errors come from the file extension. Fix: click the pencil icon on the dataset, open Datatypes and set fastqsanger.gz for the Eucalyptus R1, R2 and nanopore files. The edit is blocked while a job is still using that dataset, so wait or rerun the job afterwards.

## Jobs stay queued or take a long time

The public server is shared. Flye needed 15 to 20 minutes or more, and several of our jobs were still running after a long time. Plan for waiting, and start the slow steps first. Galaxy keeps a record of each job's run time in the dataset details.

## I cannot open the practice history

Use the shared link, choose Import this history, and copy only the active datasets. The history then appears among your histories and can be used as a starting point.

## Workflows do not appear after import

Go to Workflows, Import, GA4GH servers, search for "Large Genome Assembly", and import each workflow one by one as needed. The import can take a moment.

## BUSCO shows mostly missing genes

Not necessarily an error. Check whether the input is a small subsample and whether the lineage fits the organism.

## Annotation did not run

It was not run by participants. The instructor demonstrated it to save time.
